WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.608
Mazatl’s house was very simple.

2
00:00:06.609 --> 00:00:11.286
It was made of adobe clay bricks.

3
00:00:11.287 --> 00:00:17.688
The house was one big room divided into separate areas.

4
00:00:17.689 --> 00:00:20.933
Vinnie and Mandy met Mazatl’s mother.

5
00:00:20.934 --> 00:00:24.420
She was making flat pancake-like bread.

6
00:00:24.421 --> 00:00:30.042
"These corn tortillas are for your papa," she said to Mazatl.

7
00:00:30.043 --> 00:00:34.334
"But please take a bath first."

8
00:00:34.335 --> 00:00:38.078
Mazatl led them to another building.

9
00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:41.403
"This is our bath hut," he explained.

10
00:00:41.404 --> 00:00:44.990
Vinnie and Mandy saw a mud hut.

11
00:00:44.991 --> 00:00:50.023
It had a chimney on the side with a hot fire.

12
00:00:50.024 --> 00:00:52.940
"The chimney heats the walls inside.

13
00:00:52.941 --> 00:00:55.359
We throw water on the walls.

14
00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.625
And we get lots of steam.

15
00:00:57.626 --> 00:01:03.552
We come here to get clean, but also when we are sick," Mazatl explained.

16
00:01:03.553 --> 00:01:07.338
"Does it make you better?" asked Mandy.

17
00:01:07.339 --> 00:01:10.411
"Oh yes!" replied Mazatl.

18
00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:13.640
"I once had bad pains in my chest.

19
00:01:13.641 --> 00:01:16.897
The steam and heat made me well again.

20
00:01:16.898 --> 00:01:21.558
You go first," he said to Mandy.

21
00:01:21.559 --> 00:01:24.805
Mandy had a quick steam bath.

22
00:01:24.806 --> 00:01:26.561
So did Vinnie.

23
00:01:26.562 --> 00:01:30.666
When they came out, Mazatl had fresh clothes for them.

24
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:35.474
Vinnie got a short skirt and a cloak to wear over one shoulder.

25
00:01:35.475 --> 00:01:41.278
Mandy got a colorful sleeveless shirt and a skirt.

26
00:01:41.279 --> 00:01:45.751
"My mother and sister wove these clothes," Mazatl said.

27
00:01:45.752 --> 00:01:48.282
"You can return them later."

28
00:01:48.283 --> 00:01:53.475
"Thank you, they’re beautiful," replied Mandy.

29
00:01:53.476 --> 00:01:59.559
Then Mazatl bathed and changed too.

30
00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:05.811
"Mazatl and his family are so nice," Mandy whispered to her brother.

31
00:02:05.812 --> 00:02:11.283
"I can’t believe the Aztecs make human sacrifices."

32
00:02:11.284 --> 00:02:15.622
Vinnie didn’t want to think about it.

33
00:02:15.623 --> 00:02:22.308
Taking the tortillas from his mother, Mazatl led Vinnie and Mandy to a canoe.

34
00:02:22.309 --> 00:02:25.089
They got to the crowded market.

35
00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:29.354
Vinnie and Mandy were amazed!

36
00:02:29.355 --> 00:02:34.577
People arrived in canoes or carried their goods on their backs.

37
00:02:34.578 --> 00:02:38.548
They could hear voices arguing loudly.

38
00:02:38.549 --> 00:02:42.158
"I need to find my papa," said Mazatl.

39
00:02:42.159 --> 00:02:50.406
They walked past people selling many interesting things.

40
00:02:50.407 --> 00:02:53.003
"Are those bear skins?"

41
00:02:53.004 --> 00:02:56.962
Mandy asked, pointing to a stack of fur.

42
00:02:56.963 --> 00:03:00.737
"Bears? Those are puma and jaguar skins.

43
00:03:00.738 --> 00:03:06.008
Only the rich can afford them," Mazatl explained.

44
00:03:06.009 --> 00:03:10.872
Vinnie also noticed a man holding a bag of something.

45
00:03:10.873 --> 00:03:17.690
"I will give you three rabbits for those cocoa beans!" a buyer yelled at the man.

46
00:03:17.691 --> 00:03:23.347
"Give me five rabbits and two geese," the seller shouted back.

47
00:03:23.348 --> 00:03:25.085
"Are you mad?

48
00:03:25.086 --> 00:03:29.803
I don’t have that many animals!" the buyer screamed.

49
00:03:29.804 --> 00:03:31.894
"I’m offering you a bargain!

50
00:03:31.895 --> 00:03:37.002
Take it or leave it!" the seller shouted.

51
00:03:37.003 --> 00:03:40.560
"Oh, no!" Mandy said.

52
00:03:40.561 --> 00:03:44.144
"I think those two men are going to fight."

53
00:03:44.145 --> 00:03:49.058
Mazatl laughed and said, "Don’t worry.

54
00:03:49.059 --> 00:03:51.287
The judges are watching them."

55
00:03:51.288 --> 00:03:54.951
"Judges?" asked Vinnie.

56
00:03:54.952 --> 00:03:58.401
Just then a tall man walked over.

57
00:03:58.402 --> 00:04:01.477
He said a few words to the buyer.

58
00:04:01.478 --> 00:04:04.350
The man nodded and walked away.

59
00:04:04.351 --> 00:04:09.157
"Our judges are wise and fair," Mazatl said.

60
00:04:09.158 --> 00:04:13.985
"What exactly do the judges do?" asked Vinnie.

61
00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.397
Mazatl looked at his new friends strangely.

62
00:04:17.398 --> 00:04:20.818
"Judges make sure people behave fairly.

63
00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:23.342
We must obey what they say.

64
00:04:23.343 --> 00:04:29.317
Surely you know that."

